  "summary": "Malicious code in tinkoff-statist-browser-typed-client-art.apps.reporegistry (npm)",
  "details": "On require(), the package fingerprints the host OS and architecture, then downloads a platform-specific binary payload from Cloudflare Workers C2 endpoints (oob-worker[.]cf100-416[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf99-9b3[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf101-adf[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf102-baf[.]workers[.]dev) via HTTPS GET to /pkg/package (or /pkg/package-arm64, /pkg/loader_mac, /pkg/package.exe depending on platform). If HTTPS fails, it falls back to DNS TXT-record reassembly from c[.]tin[.]dl[.]well1[.]site. The downloaded binary is written to /var/tmp/.cache_\u003crandom_hex\u003e (Linux/macOS) or C:\\Windows\\Temp\\dotnet_diag_\u003crandom_hex\u003e.exe (Windows) and executed as a detached background process. The package ships a large decoy analytics SDK (lib/telemetry.js) to appear legitimate.",
